---
model: claude
prompt:
  schemaStrictness: retry
permissions:
  # A plan run is read-only investigation, so it states its whole posture here
  # rather than leaving it to Go: an unstated posture is filled in with the edit
  # preset and the full edit toolset, which is the opposite of what plan means.
  mode: plan
  tools:
    Read: allow
    Glob: allow
    Grep: allow
---
{{#if multiple}}You are planning the implementation of the {{count}} todo items listed below. Produce ONE plan that covers all of them.{{else}}You are planning the implementation of the todo item below in this codebase.{{/if}}

{{{body}}}---
## Instructions

You are running in plan mode: investigate the codebase read-only and author a complete implementation plan. Do NOT modify any source files.

1. Explore the code paths the todo touches; understand the root cause or design before planning.
2. Include the full step-by-step implementation plan in the final StructuredOutput call's top-level `planContent` field: the files to change, new types/functions and their signatures, what gets deleted, the testing strategy, and risks.
3. If your native plan mode also created a readable plan file, report its ABSOLUTE path in `planPath`. Do not try to write a file in a read-only sandbox. Gavel persists the complete plan content for human review.
{{#if existingPlan}}
4. An earlier plan for this todo already exists (below). Re-evaluate it against the current code: if it still stands as written, report top-level `planStatus` "unchanged"; if it needs revision, report the revised plan and `planStatus` "updated".

## Existing Plan

{{{existingPlan}}}
{{else}}
4. This todo has no prior plan; author one and report top-level `planStatus` "new".
{{/if}}

The final StructuredOutput call carries `summary`, `endStatus`, `planStatus`, and the full `planContent` as separate top-level fields. Include `planPath` only when the file exists and is readable. Never JSON-encode an object or another field value into a string.

If you are blocked on a decision only a human can make, stop and report endStatus "ask" with your questions in the final result instead of guessing.
